---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const updated = 'October 19, 2026';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="How Load Plan Calc handles data, cookies and advertising.">
  <section>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="small">Last updated {updated}</p>
    <p class="lede">We collect as little as possible. We have no accounts, no sign-ups and no forms that send your data to us.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Calculators</h2>
    <p>Our calculators run in your browser. Your unit choice may be stored in your own browser's local storage, and the plan you enter is kept in the page address so you can share it. Nothing you type is sent to us.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Advertising and cookies</h2>
    <p>This site is supported by advertising served by Google AdSense. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this website or other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visits to this site and/or other sites on the Internet.</p>
    <p>You may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="nofollow">Google Ads Settings</a>. You can also opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalized advertising at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="nofollow">www.aboutads.info</a>. To learn how Google uses information from sites that use its services, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="nofollow">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>.</p>
    <p>Visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland are asked for consent before personalized ads or advertising cookies are used, through a consent message shown on the site. You can change your choice at any time from the link in that message.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Site statistics</h2>
    <p>We use Google Analytics to understand how the site is used: which pages are read, roughly where visitors come from (country and the site or search engine that referred them), and the type of device and browser. Google Analytics sets first-party cookies (named <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>) to tell visits apart. It does not tell us who you are, and we do not send it names, email addresses or anything you type into our calculators.</p>
    <p>In the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland, these cookies are not set unless you give consent. Elsewhere you can block them in your browser settings or with the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="nofollow">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Server logs</h2>
    <p>Like any website, our hosting provider processes technical data such as IP addresses to deliver pages and protect the site from abuse.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct or delete personal data and to object to its use. Because we do not hold personal data about visitors ourselves, most requests are best directed to Google through the links above. For anything else, email <a href="mailto:contact@loadplancalc.com">contact@loadplancalc.com</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>This site is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect their information.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If we change this policy, we will update the date at the top of this page.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
